<concept importance="optional" id="t00172">
	<title>High Beam Assist (HBA)</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>lighting
					<indexterm>high beam assist (HBA)</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01088">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e01089">
								<image href="images/N_SP327_B10_021.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>The HBA function automatically adjusts the headlight range (switches between high beam and low beam) depending on the brightness of detected vehicles and certain road conditions.</p>
		<section>
			<title>Detection sensor</title>
			<p>Please refer to <xref href="t00444.dita#t00444"/> for the applicable sensors and their locations.</p>
			<note type="tip">
				<ul>
					<li>
						<p>Always keep the front view camera in good condition to maintain optimal performance of High Beam Assist.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p>For more information about the front view camera, refer to <xref href="t00445.dita#t00445"/>.</p>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</note>
		</section>
	</conbody>
